# per-leaf-manifest — allow/exclude list for per-leaf verify-merged (issue #194 / F-A / I2)
#
# Criterion for ALLOW: verdict = pure function of merged content; no launcher loops,
# no background processes, no timing/poll/sleep asserts, no recursive verify-merged.
#
# Criterion for EXCLUDE (default-fail-safe): anything not meeting the above criterion.
# New/unknown/unclassified test ⇒ NOT in ALLOW ⇒ excluded from per-leaf by default.
# GHA engine job (ci.yml:21-33) runs the FULL suite regardless of this manifest.
#
# Guard: reference/tests/leaf-verifier.test.sh verifies:
#   union(ALLOW, EXCLUDE) == all reference/tests/*.test.sh (currently 45 total)
#   ALLOW ∩ EXCLUDE = ∅
#   ALLOW = 10, EXCLUDE = 35
# A new unclassified *.test.sh causes the guard to RED (fail-closed / drift prevention).
#
# Format: ALLOW <basename>  or  EXCLUDE <basename>  (basename = without .test.sh suffix)

ALLOW acceptance-block
ALLOW cli-smoke
ALLOW gate-comment-payload
ALLOW launchable
ALLOW manifest-lib
ALLOW marker-gate
ALLOW prep-params
ALLOW runtime-lint
ALLOW spawn-unit
ALLOW token-hygiene

